.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-check
.Nd check a sealed capsule folder against its seal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis check
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis check
checks the capsule
.Ar dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
it reads and checks the seal
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
checks that the SHA-256 of
.Pa noqtis.json
is the one in the seal, verifies the signature over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json ,
then lists the folder and checks every listed file (present, a regular
file, the size, the SHA-256 and the SHA3-256) and that no file is present
that the manifest does not list.
.Pp
It prints one row per check: a status
.Pq Ql ok No or Ql FAIL ,
the check's name and a detail, then a summary line
.Dl <dir>: OK (<n> checks passed)
or
.Dl <dir>: FAILED (<k> of <n> checks failed)
.Pp
Without
.Fl p ,
the public key inside the seal is accepted: the check then shows that the
files are those the key holder sealed, not who the key holder is.
The
.Ql key
row says so, and a note on standard error says to pass
.Fl p .
With
.Fl p ,
the seal's key must be exactly the given key.
.Pp
A seal that carries a timestamp fails its
.Ql timestamp
row here, because this command takes no TSA trust anchors to check it
with; a timestamp that cannot be checked is never passed silently.
Programs that need timestamps call
.Xr nqchkt 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
The public signature key the capsule must be sealed with.
.It Fl j , Fl -json
Print one line of JSON instead of the table:
.Bd -literal
{"capsule":"<dir>","ok":<bool>,"result":"<nqerr text>",
 "checks":[{"check":"<name>","ok":<bool>,"detail":"<text>"},...]}
.Ed
.El
.Ss Checks
The row names are stable, for scripts:
.Bl -tag -width "manifest.canonical"
.It Cm seal.read
.Pa noqtis.sig
exists, is a regular file (not a link) and is at most 1 MiB.
.It Cm seal.parse , seal.canonical
It is a JSON object in canonical form (RFC 8785).
.It Cm seal.fields
It has exactly the fields of
.Ql noqtis-seal-1 ,
with the right types;
.Ql manifest_sha256
is 64 lower-case hex digits.
.It Cm seal.format
.Ql format
is
.Ql noqtis-seal-1 .
.It Cm seal.alg
.Ql alg
names a signature algorithm noqtis knows.
.It Cm seal.context
.Ql context
is at most 255 bytes.
.It Cm seal.key , seal.signature
.Ql public_key
and
.Ql signature
are base64 of the algorithm's sizes.
.It Cm manifest.read
.Pa noqtis.json
exists, is a regular file and is at most 512 MiB.
.It Cm manifest.digest
Its SHA-256 is the seal's
.Ql manifest_sha256 .
.It Cm key
Whether the key was pinned with
.Fl p .
.It Cm signature
The signature verifies over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json .
.It Cm timestamp
Present only when the seal has a timestamp (or anchors were given).
.It Cm folder
The folder could be listed within the limits.
.It Cm file
One row per listed file.
.It Cm manifest.parse , manifest.canonical , manifest.fields
The manifest is canonical JSON with exactly the fields of
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 .
.It Cm manifest.format , manifest.created , manifest.order
.Ql format
is
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 ,
.Ql created
is an RFC 3339 UTC time, and the files are sorted by path with no repeats.
.It Cm path
One row per refused, non-normal, duplicate or too long path, and per two
paths that differ only in case.
.It Cm extra
One row per regular file present but not listed.
.It Cm unsafe
One row per link, reparse point, special file or refused name in the
folder.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
Every check passed.
.It 1
A check failed (the files changed, the seal or manifest is damaged or not
signed by
.Ar key.pub ) .
.It 2
A usage error,
.Ar dir
does not exist, a key that is not a public signature key, or a library
error such as running out of memory.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results
      check               detail
ok    seal.read           noqtis.sig
\&...
ok    signature           ML-DSA-65 signature over noqtis.json is valid
ok    folder              listed
ok    file                data/in.csv
ok    file                report.txt
\&...
ok    manifest.order      files sorted by path, no repeats
results: OK (22 checks passed)
.Ed
.Pp
After a file was changed and one added:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results; echo $?
\&...
FAIL  file                report.txt: size differs
\&...
FAIL  extra               new.txt: not in the manifest
results: FAILED (2 of 23 checks failed)
1
.Ed
.Pp
In CI, keeping only the failed rows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check --json -p me.pub results |
    jq -r '.checks[] | select(.ok | not) | .detail'
report.txt: size differs
new.txt: not in the manifest
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqchkt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
